\fs32\b Keyboard Shortcuts\b0\fs20\par
\par
WinBMD2 provides keyboard shortcuts which allow many common transcription operations to be performed without using the mouse.\par
\par
\b F1\b0  - Display WinBMD2 Help.\par
\par
\fs24\b Moving around the transcription grid\b0\fs20\par
\b Tab\b0  - Move to the next field.\par
\par
\b Enter\b0  - Move to the next field.\par
\par
\b Shift+Tab\b0  - Move to the previous field.\par
\par
\b Up Arrow / Down Arrow\b0  - Move to the cell above or below.\par
\par
\b Alt+Up Arrow / Alt+Down Arrow\b0  - When a picklist is displayed, move the selection up or down through the picklist.\par
\par
\b Ctrl+Up Arrow / Ctrl+Down Arrow\b0  - Move the scan by one transcription row.\par
\par
\fs24\b Entering information\b0\fs20\par
\b F4\b0  - Display the special-character selector while entering a field.\par
\par
\b F9\b0  - Clear the current cell.\par
\par
\b 1 to 9\b0  - When a picklist is displayed, select the corresponding item from the list.\par
\par
\b Numeric keypad 1 to 9\b0  - Select the corresponding item from a displayed picklist.\par
\par
\fs24\b General\b0\fs20\par
Many operations in WinBMD2 can also be performed using the command buttons above the transcription grid.\par
\par
The shortcuts available while entering information may depend on the current field and whether a picklist or other entry aid is being displayed.\par
}